  "rationale": "PINS the `references` edge for a function's RESULT TYPES in BOTH shapes the grammar allows. tree-sitter-go's node-types.json gives a function/method/func_literal a `result` field that is EITHER one type node (`type_identifier`, `pointer_type`, `slice_type`, `map_type`, `channel_type`, `qualified_type`, `function_type`) OR a `parameter_list`. Go's spec writes a single result with no parentheses and two or more inside them, so the parenthesised form reaches the `parameter_declaration` case in extractDeclaredTypeRefs and the BARE form reached no case at all. Measured over a 200-file stride sample of go-stdlib: 262 bare-result sites in 46 files produced 265 expected edges and 1 published (0.4%); 156 parenthesised sites in 33 files produced 167 expected and 162 published (97.0%). The bare form is Go's dominant signature spelling, so this is the majority of the surface and it was silent. Rows are authored from the grammar and the spec; the line numbers come from this file's own text.",
